{
  "about": "The speech models Kryakl can use, read by the engine (asr.py) and by Kryakl (src/speechplan.ts). rank: how accurate, higher is better, used for a language not in errors; errors: words wrong in a hundred per language as Kryakl dictates, clean and with a fan, measured by engine/quality on 2026-11-11 (docs/speech-quality.md). phrase: seconds to recognize a 7 s phrase as Dictate does; rtf: seconds per second of a long recording as Transcribe does (words with their times). Both are first guesses, measured on an i9-9900K (cpu, int8) and an RTX 2080 SUPER (cuda, float16) on 2026-10-28, until this computer is tested. Whisper pads every phrase to a 30 s window, so a phrase costs one window whatever its length; turbo's decoder is light, so on long recordings it is nearly as quick as small. ramMb: memory on the processor; vramMb: on the card, per compute type. Parakeet (NVIDIA's TDT 0.6B v3 through onnx-asr, int8, on the processor) costs what the sound lasts, not a window: a 7 s phrase in 0.3 s on the i9; it dictates in its 25 languages. On the bench (2026-11-11) it makes about one and a half times turbo's errors (Russian 7.6 against 5.0, Ukrainian 16.9 against 10.0 words wrong in a hundred), as many as small but seven times quicker on the processor, so its rank is under turbo's. devices and features: where and for what a model is used.",
